{"message": "I have localized the issue to the sign-in magic code flow. The bug is in `src/pages/signin/ValidateCodeForm/BaseValidateCodeForm.tsx`: the `resendValidateCode` function (triggered by clicking "Didn't receive a magic code") only calls `User.resendValidateCode(...)` and resets the countdown timer, but never resets/focuses the `MagicCodeInput` ref. Unlike the equivalent `resendValidateCode` handlers in `src/components/ValidateCodeActionModal/ValidateCodeForm/BaseValidateCodeForm.tsx`, `src/pages/settings/Profile/Contacts/ValidateCodeForm/BaseValidateCodeForm.tsx`, and `src/pages/settings/Security/AddDelegate/ValidateCodeForm/BaseValidateCodeForm.tsx` (which call `inputValidateCodeRef.current.clear()` / `.focus()`), it does not call `inputValidateCodeRef.current.clear()` (or `resetFocus()`), so focus remains on the digit the user had shifted to instead of returning to the first digit.

The `MagicCodeInput` component (`src/components/MagicCodeInput.tsx`) already exposes the needed imperative handles — `clear()` (resets to index 0 and focuses), `resetFocus()`, and `focus()` — so the fix belongs in the sign-in form's `resendValidateCode`, with supporting validation in `src/libs/ValidationUtils.ts` (`isValidValidateCode`) and the actual resend/sign-in actions in `src/libs/actions/Session/index.ts` (`resendValidateCode`, `signInWithValidateCode`) and `src/libs/actions/User.ts` (`resendValidateCode`).

